[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Queen's Gambit Accepted: Normal Variation, 3...Bg4"]
[ECO "D21"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "regain-the-pawn,transposition"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3...Bg4"]
[Start "accepted 3.Nf3"]

3... Bg4 { Pins the knight on f3 and develops the bishop before ...e6 shuts it in. } ( 3... Nc6 { The same position as the Chigorin Defence after 3...dxc4: White plays e3 and takes back on c4. } ) ( 3... b5 4. e3 { Opens the bishop on f1. Black's pawns on b5 and c4 will be undermined with a4. } 4... e6 ( 4... c6 { The same position as the Slav after 3...dxc4 4.e3 b5. } ) 5. a4 c6 { The same position as the Slav after 3...dxc4 4.e3 b5: White plays axb5 and b3. } ) ( 3... Bf5 4. e3 e6 ( 4... Nf6 5. Bxc4 e6 ) 5. Bxc4 Nf6 6. O-O { Castles. Plan: Nc3 and Qe2, then e4 to hit the bishop on f5. } ) 4. e3 { The usual plan: open the bishop on f1 and take back on c4. } 4... Nf6 ( 4... e6 5. Bxc4 Nf6 ) 5. Bxc4 e6 6. Nc3 Nbd7 7. O-O Be7 8. h3 { Asks the bishop. Taking on f3 gives White the two bishops; going back to h5 leaves it far from the queenside. } 8... Bh5 9. e4 { Takes the centre now that the pieces are out. Plan: Be3, Qe2 and Rad1, then push d5 or e5. } *
